<BaseLayout title="AI Systems Reliability Lab — Evaluation, diagnosis & authority" description="A focused technical-proof program for frozen AI release evaluation, bounded failure forensics, routing constraints, and explicit human-authority checks.">
  <article class="lab-case-study">
    <header class="lab-hero shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Focused technical proof · Reliability Lab</p>
      <h1>Evaluate the release.<br />Diagnose the failure. Authorize the action.</h1>
      <p class="lab-subtitle">A focused program of bounded AI reliability experiments: evaluate whether a candidate configuration earns release, diagnose where a bad outcome began, route only when quality permits it, and authorize bounded action explicitly.</p>
      <p class="lab-summary">Prove the controls before granting more authority. Labs 01–02 evaluate and diagnose; Lab 03 closed its Freeze A route set when no router was needed; Lab 04 tests explicit human-authority requirements before bounded synthetic execution.</p>
      <p class="lab-cta">
