    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-one">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">02 · Lab 01</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-one">A frozen release decision remained visible after the evaluator was audited.</h2>
<p>Lab 01 compared two frozen configurations across 30 synthetic cases. Both passed deterministic validation, but the historical automated release decision was <strong>FAIL</strong>: the candidate’s 58.6% factual-support score remained below the frozen 90% threshold.</p>
<div class="lab-method-grid">
<div>
<strong>Frozen experiment</strong>
<span>30 cases · both configurations 30 / 30 deterministic checks · 0 regressions.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Human audit</strong>
<span>60 / 60 outputs reviewed. The candidate was materially weaker, and the local semantic evaluator had not earned release authority.</span>
</div>
</div>
<table class="lab-comparison">
<caption>Lab 01 human-audit comparison</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Measure</th>
<th scope="col">Baseline</th>
<th scope="col">Candidate</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Human-confirmed factual support</th>
<td>96.7%</td>
<td>70.0%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Judge / human agreement</th>
<td>53.3%</td>
<td>43.3%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p class="lab-note">Human review added interpretation without rewriting the historical automated FAIL.</p>
</div>
</section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-two">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">03 · Lab 02</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-two">A final bad brief may be a downstream symptom—not the root cause.</h2>
<p>Lab 02 is a frozen synthetic fixture with five stages: <strong>Normalize → Classify → Select evidence → Recommend → Generate final brief</strong>. It records inspectable intermediate state and structured traces so the first causal failure can be distinguished from where the outcome became visible.</p>
</div>
</section>

