    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-causality">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">04 · Causality</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-causality">The stage where a problem appears is not necessarily the stage that caused it.</h2>
<ol class="lab-decision-chain">
<li>
<strong>Propagated</strong>
<span>An earlier invalid state was actually consumed by a later stage and observed in its output.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Contained</strong>
<span>A failed stage stopped later work fail-closed; blocked stages were not treated as propagated failures.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Local</strong>
<span>The failure had no invalid downstream output.</span>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Root cause</strong>
<span>A classification defect can produce evidence, recommendation, and final-brief symptoms; final generation is not automatically the cause.</span>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="lab-note">The canonical <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/ai-systems-reliability-lab/blob/main/labs/02-failure-forensics/results/failure_lineage.svg">failure-lineage visual <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a> shows this distinction in the technical evidence record.</p>
</div>
</section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-three">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">05 · Lab 03</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-three">The routing experiment stopped when complexity did not earn its place.</h2>
<p>For the frozen Freeze A V002 route definitions and six-case canary, R0 was eligible 6 / 6 while R1 and R2 were ineligible 0 / 6. The capability gradient was absent, so the disposition was <strong>NO-ROUTER-NEEDED</strong>, supported only for that frozen route set.</p>
<div class="lab-method-grid">
<div>
<strong>Quality first</strong>
<span>Quality is a constraint before cost is an optimization target.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Bounded conclusion</strong>
<span>Freeze B and its 36 measured cases were not authorized; the result does not claim routing is generally useless.</span>
</div>
</div>
<p class="lab-note">Complexity must pay rent. The experiment stopped rather than manufacturing a routing comparison.</p>
</div>
</section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-four">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">06 · Lab 04</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-four">A declared human requirement was enforced before bounded synthetic execution.</h2>
<p>Lab 04 tested whether explicit human-authority requirements could be enforced before a bounded synthetic action reached execution. The frozen 12-case matrix passed with zero unauthorized executions.</p>
<div class="lab-method-grid">
<div>
<strong>Decision types</strong>
<span>AUTONOMOUS, HUMAN_REQUIRED, and PROHIBITED are distinct; the experiment does not claim every action requires human approval.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Frozen result</strong>
<span>0 disposition, reason-code, authority-requirement, or executor-state mismatches; safety and correctness were not falsified.</span>
</div>
</div>
<p class="lab-note">Synthetic, deterministic, local, and standard-library only: no model, database, external service, or real message. Authorization present ≠ authorization valid; valid authorization ≠ unbounded authority.</p>
</div>
</section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-judgment">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">07 · Human judgment</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-judgment">Mechanically plausible evidence did not earn publication authority.</h2>
<p>Matthew designed the forensic experiment around causal failure localization, required inspectable intermediate state and real stage-to-stage consumption, rejected a mechanically plausible but causally weak first publication candidate, and directed the repaired experiment and validation against stricter evidence requirements.</p>
<div class="lab-authorship">
<div>
<strong>Causality, not sequence</strong>
<span>Stage order alone did not prove propagation; actual downstream consumption had to be observed.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Containment, not propagation</strong>
<span>Fail-closed blocking was distinguished from an invalid state that had travelled downstream.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Repair direction</strong>
<span>The experiment was repaired to consume real accumulated stage state rather than assign propagation mechanically.</span>
</div>
<div>
<strong>Regression preservation</strong>
<span>`evidence-01` fails at evidence selection before its bounded correction and passes after it; the loop remains a regression test.</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-boundary">
<div class="lab-label">
<p class="eyebrow">08 · Boundaries</p>
</div>
<div class="lab-body">
<h2 id="lab-boundary">Small, inspectable experiments—not a production claim.</h2>
<div class="lab-boundaries">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">What this demonstrates</p>
<ul>
<li>Frozen evaluation and deterministic failure analysis</li>
<li>Structured traces and bounded causal localization</li>
<li>Evidence integrity and explicit human authority</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">What this does not claim</p>
<ul>
<li>Production incident forensics or observability ownership</li>
<li>Live model monitoring or autonomous remediation</li>
<li>Generalized diagnostic accuracy or enterprise-scale operation</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<p class="lab-note">Lab 02 is synthetic, deterministic, and local. It invokes no model, reports token fields as unavailable, and incurred $0 API/service spend. Its 1.656 ms measurement is fixture execution timing—not model inference or production latency.</p>
</div>
</section>

